MID_SE_Esm_Lys_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_C_001: It's no use. This is impenetrable to me.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_C_002: Lysander! I thought I recognized you over here.\nWhat's up? Something bothering you?
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_C_003: Esmeralda? Of all the people who could have\nhappened by, it had to be you.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_C_004: What did you just say? I came over just to talk to\nyou! This is what I get for trying to be nice?
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_C_005: That much, I apologize for. But let me be plain—\nI find you difficult to be around.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_C_006: You put no respect on Her Majesty or Yu Phas's\nnames, no matter how many times I scold you.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_C_007: I'm not going to correct myself for things that aren't\nmistakes. Theodora's Theodora! To me, anyway.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_C_008: Rrrgh. As you will. My more pressing problem is\nthe letter I received from a woman.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_C_009: Being from Saramis, where the written word is\nforbidden, I don't know what she meant to convey.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_C_010: So you should go ask her?
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_C_011: If I could, this would be so much simpler. But she\nwas a stranger who dashed off after delivering it.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_C_012: But I'm certain this letter contains profound feelings.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_C_013: Why, when I asked passersby, they brushed me off as\nsoon as they saw it. Some had very unkind laughs.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_C_014: So there's a girl out there even for you! I was\nwondering if your personality put them off.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_C_015: How insufferably rude you are! I was a fool to even\nconsider asking you for a favor.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_C_016: To allow one of such base character to give voice to\nthe words within would be an insult to the writer!
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_C_017: Rude? You're rude! Why does it matter who reads it,\nas long as it gets read?
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_C_018: It does not—so long as that person is not you! How\ndare you impugn the honor of a Saraminian warrior?!
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_C_019: Haaah... Haaah... Damn! He got away! Next time\nhe'll be— What's that?
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_C_020: Well look at this! He dropped his little note. I had\nbetter read it while I have the chance!
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_C_021: Wait just a second. This is not a love letter!
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_001: Hey... Lysander? Remember this letter? You\ndropped it.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_002: You had it all this time?! I've been searching for\nit everywhere.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_003: Aren't you going to thank me for finding it? Eh,\nanyway. It's not what you thought it was.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_004: You've read it? Fine, then. Tell me what it\nactually says.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_005: It just goes on and on about Yu Phas—how she was\nexecuted as an evil goddess and should stay gone.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_006: What?! Disrespect is one thing, but I will not brook\nthis outright slander!
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_007: OK. So first, I wouldn't lie about this. Second, if I had\nsomething to say, I'd say it to your face.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_008: Yes...that is consistent with your character. Then\nsomeone else is defaming my goddess. Unacceptable!
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_009: Funny that you use that word—unacceptable. That's\nthe same thing she said. About her father's death.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_010: She says he'd been sick for a long time, fighting as\nhard as he could—till the goddess claimed his soul.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_011: That is not Yu Phas's way. She is kindness itself—\nshe saved the lives of our ancestors!
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_012: That's how people in your country see it, right? But\nnot everyone does. I thought you knew.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_013: Why did you bring this to me? To mock me?\nAnother outsider sticking her nose in?
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_014: Why are you taking it out on me? Why are you even\nangry at all?
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_015: Yu Phas is the victim here, not you! She's dead, and\npeople are still fighting over her.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_016: You hate it when people say bad stuff, they hate it\nwhen you say good stuff. That's all this is.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_017: If it was me you were fighting over, I'd be like, "You\nguys hash it out. Leave me out of it."
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_018: You really are arrogant to compare yourself to\na goddess.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_019: Yep, that's me. Anyway, I said what I had to say, so\nI'll be off.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_020: A moment, please. What you said was true. Rather\nthan take offense, I should speak with her.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_021: My father is also no longer with us. So I understand\nher sorrow, to a degree.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_022: I am well aware she may not want to talk to me,\nbut there must be a way.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_023: Well, good. You may be uptight, and have a stick\ncrammed RIGHT up there, but you're an OK guy.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_024: Come on, then. I figured out where she lives.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_025: Really?!
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_026: Sure. I got her father's name from the letter and\nasked around. It wasn't hard.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_027: I was already planning to go talk to her—whether\nyou wanted to come or not.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_B_028: Haha... You are a handful. I am much obliged.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_001: That cheered her up! I mean, after she got over the\nshock of two strangers showing up at her door.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_002: That was to be expected. I imagine she didn't think\nshe'd ever see me again.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_003: "I'm not here on behalf of Saramis. I speak only for\nmyself." And it worked!
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_004: Your presence as a neutral observer helped. I'm glad\nwe could support her after she lost her only family.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_005: Esmeralda, I must thank you again. I could never\nhave done this without you.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_006: When we crossed paths that day, I held an unfair\ngrudge in my heart. I misjudged you.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_007: I now see our chance meeting that day as a blessing.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_008: You really were a jerk. But come on—anybody could\nhave helped you out here.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_009: Untrue. Remember that none of the passersby would\nhelp me read the letter.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_010: I suspect some were afraid of voicing anti-Yu Phas\nsentiments in front of a Saraminian.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_011: Others sympathized with the girl and sneered at\nmy illiteracy.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_012: Only you acted without prejudice towards me, her,\nor my goddess.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_013: That's me—I'm honest. Everybody should try it.\nImagine a world like that!
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_014: There is such a thing as too much honesty. Though,\nwhile we are on the subject, one last thing.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_015: I had forgotten before this incident that there was\na time when I myself loathed Yu Phas.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_016: Really? I did not expect this one.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_017: It was when I learned of my father's death in the\nwar. I was still very young, and I blamed her.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_018: I thought my father had done as the prayer says—\noffered his soul to Yu Phas in battle.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_019: I howled my resentment, asking "Has Father died to\nrepay our ancestors' debt?!" I was a fool.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_020: No, you weren't. You were blind. We all can be,\nwhen our feelings get in the way.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_021: That is exactly how it was for me. But my mother\nexplained my error.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_022: Our loving goddess saved our ancestors. So Father's\nsoul was also received in her warm embrace.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_023: At the moment of his death, Father knew peace.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_024: I felt clarity return to me then. And ever since,\nI have loved Yu Phas as she loves us.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_025: But if not for my mother's words, my anger and spite\nfor Yu Phas might have persisted to this day.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_026: The same as that girl. That's why you were able to\ntalk to her—because you'd felt the same pain.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_027: I can only hope I connected with her. If we did,\nas I said, I owe it to you.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_028: I will continue to lend an ear to any voices who\ncurse my goddess. It may be my calling.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_029: Good. You don't have to be a goddess to see that it's\nbetter to make friends than enemies.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_030: Ahaha! Your forthright, optimistic brand of\nrudeness is growing on me.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_031: Well, you're still a total stick in the mud... But if you\nneed my help, just ask. Anytime.
MID_SE_Esm_Lys_A_032: I promise that I will. May we both find new ways\nto support the other.